      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\n`KimiAudioTokenizer` registers only 6 hardcoded tokens while `tokenizer_config.json` declares 421, and the call sites that need that set disagree: `encode()` rejects every prompt, `all_special_tokens` returns `AddedToken` objects, and streaming leaks `[EOS]`.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- `allowed_special` = config tokens ∪ the 6 hardcoded ones. On main, `encode(\"<|im_user_msg_start|>hello\")` raises `ValueError: Encountered text corresponding to disallowed special token`: 415 config tokens are registered as tiktoken special tokens but not allowed, and the chat template emits them.\r\n- `all_special_tokens` returns `list[str]`; `AddedToken` never compares equal to a token string and made `_build_drop_info` raise `TypeError` on every parser-engine stream.\r\n- `convert_ids_to_tokens(skip_special_tokens=True)` skips the same ids as `decode()`, using one `frozenset` built in `__init__` (no per-token rebuild).\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n`pytest tests/tokenizers_/test_kimi_audio.py -v` — 3 of 4 assertions fail on main, all pass here. Against `moonshotai/Kimi-Audio-7B-Instruct`:\r\n\r\n- `detokenize_incrementally` per step: 5.78 µs → 5.52 µs\r\n- `encode(\"<|im_user_msg_start|>hello\")`: `ValueError` → `[151646, 14990]`\r\n- streaming with `skip_special_tokens=True`: leaks `[EOS]` → clean\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- Special-token strings in the prompt are now encoded instead of raising, as in HF tokenizers. `encode()` costs ~68 µs vs ~32 µs per call (tiktoken rebuilds its matcher over 421 strings); once per request.\r\n- Known gap: `convert_tokens_to_ids` / `skip_special_tokens=False` still only know the 6 hardcoded tokens, so the rest come back as `<|unk|>`. Visible only when a client sets `skip_special_tokens=False` (default `True`).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** new unit test exercises the public tokenizer API in CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` pass; no user-visible docs needed.\r\n</details>",
